  "id": "DrugBank_DB00327 - MONDO_5709",
  "verbalization": "Hydromorphone is implicated in the pathogenesis of the Common Cold through a chain of indications that link it to Nasopharyngitis, a condition associated with the Cold. The evidence suggests that Hydromorphone may be used in the treatment or management of Nasopharyngitis, which in turn is linked to the Common Cold. This relationship is supported by the presence of multiple pathways where Hydromorphone is associated with Nasopharyngitis, and Nasopharyngitis is associated with the Common Cold. The shared indication of Nasopharyngitis across different pathways indicates a potential functional or biological link between Hydromorphone and the development or manifestation of the Common Cold. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role of Hydromorphone in the inflammatory or symptomatic management of Nasopharyngitis, which could contribute to the development of the Common Cold. The evidence suggests that the relationship between Hydromorphone and the Common Cold is mediated through Nasopharyngitis, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
